  "query_preview": "/SATURDAY THROUGH NEXT WEEK/...\nModels continue to trend away from any organized disturbance\naffecting the Desert Southwest early next week, so it is looking\nlike the quiet weather will persist through the weekend and \nthrough at least the first half of next week. Short-wave ridging \nis expected to move through this weekend before a very weak \nshortwave is favored to skim by just to our north on Monday. \nConsiderable drying Friday into Saturday is expected to result in \na dry air mass lasting into early next week keeping clear to \nmostly clear skies in place. Despite the quiet weather conditions \nand passing ridge, temperatures should stay slightly below normal \nover the weekend and into early next week with lower desert highs \nranging from the upper 60s to the lower 70s and lows mostly in the\n40s. \n\nUncertainty increases for the latter half of next week with a\nslight majority of the GEFS members bringing a Pacific trough \nthrough the Southwestern U.S. while the rest of the GEFS members \nand the vast majority of the EPS members maintains ridging over \nthe region. The most likely outcome for the latter half of next \nweek heavily favors continued dry conditions with a slow warming \ntrend and temperatures eventually returning to within the normal \nrange for late November.",
